    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108639" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκῡδής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>covered with shoal-water,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱαμενή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					138
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ctes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Din.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				17.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκυδεῖς τίνες εἰσί; κοῖλοι τόποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AB</u>
					312
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκυδές: ὑποφρύδιον</span>
			(leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποβρύχιον</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διακυδόμεναι</span> is
			related.</div>
